{# The v2 survey report — the document an analyst downloads.

   Session V2-WIRE (WIRING.md slice W2). A SECOND renderer over the SAME
   build_context() the markdown template renders from: render_markdown() is
   untouched, so report.md stays byte-identical and the agent keeps the exact
   reference report it has always been given.

   THREE STRUCTURAL DECISIONS, recorded here because they are the ones a
   reviewer will ask about:

   1. Reading order is the analyst's, not the template's. Summary → severity →
      finding & confidence → evidence → differential comes BEFORE the machine
      details and the analysis-parameters table. The markdown report puts those
      two between the summary and the diagnosis; an analyst reads the call
      first.
   2. ...but the gate is never buried. Doctrine is that the quality gate runs
      first and nothing downstream is valid without it, so a non-PASS verdict is
      hoisted into a ribbon directly under the masthead, above the diagnosis,
      carrying every attention line verbatim. The full 17-check roster keeps its
      own numbered section further down. The gate's SUMMARY moves up; its DETAIL
      stays where a document would put it.
   3. Absence gets a slot. An empty differential and a null trend each render a
      labelled panel saying what is absent and why. A missing damage stage and a
      missing cause section render NOTHING, because that is what the markdown
      template does and because on a misalignment report there is no "missing"
      damage stage to report — the concept does not apply.

   Sections are numbered by `ns.n`, incremented only where a section actually
   renders. #}
{% import "_v2.html.j2" as v2 %}
{% set ns = namespace(n=0) %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Vibration Survey Report — {{ machine.name }}</title>
<style>{{ stylesheet }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="doc">

{{ v2.masthead(machine) }}
{{ v2.status_banner(status_line, status_colour) }}
{# Session REPORT-3 — the gate ribbon and the webapp's notes stay ON PAGE 1,
   which is the one deliberate exception to item 1's "in this order, nothing
   else". Doctrine (structural decision 2 above) is that a non-PASS gate is
   never buried, and a degraded job's note is the thing the reader most needs
   before believing anything else on the page. Both render nothing when there
   is nothing to say, so an ordinary report's page 1 is exactly the brief's
   list. #}
{{ v2.gate_ribbon(gate, dq_notes) }}
{{ v2.notes_panel(notes) }}

{# ── PAGE 1 · the fault sheet ─────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{{ v2.fault_sheet(fault_sheet, charts, sheet_figure) }}

{# ── Everything below is Evidence, and starts on page 2 (report.css
      `.sheet { break-after: page }`). The machine summary and the severity /
      diagnosis cards moved down here from page 1: the sheet above now states
      the health line and the fault, so on page 1 they were the same claim
      twice. #}
<h2 class="evidence-head">Evidence</h2>
{{ v2.meta_strip(machine, result, analysis_parameters) }}
{{ v2.cards(ctx) }}

{# ── 1 · Summary ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<section>
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Summary") }}
  <p class="lead">{{ executive_summary | md_inline }}</p>
</section>

{# ── 2 · Severity ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<section>
{% if not_assessable %}
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Severity & coverage") }}
  {# The acceleration-only honesty block, verbatim. Added after a release
     shipped "ISO Zone A" on known-faulted, acceleration-only machines. #}
  <p><strong>What was assessed:</strong> fault detection from the spectral/envelope evidence{% if history_ran %}, plus the vibration trend over the reading history (unit-relative){% endif %}. Any findings above stand on that evidence alone.</p>
  <p><strong>What was not assessed:</strong> ISO 20816 severity — the severity rating that places the machine in a vibration band. {{ not_assessable_reason | capitalize }}, and severity is a velocity judgement, so it is left unrated. A velocity measurement (mm/s RMS, per ISO 20816) is required to establish it — see <em>Recommended Follow-up Measurements</em>.</p>
  {{ v2.zone_strip(iso, marked=false) }}
  {% if iso and iso.th_ab is not none %}
  <p class="gfx-cap">ISO zone boundaries for this machine{% if iso.threshold_note %} ({{ iso.threshold_note }}){% endif %}. <b>No value is marked</b> — severity was not assessable on this reading, so the scale is shown without a position on it.</p>
  {% endif %}
{% else %}
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Severity", iso.threshold_note if iso and iso.threshold_note else "") }}
  {{ v2.zone_strip(iso, marked=not no_diagnosis) }}
  {% if insufficient %}
  {% if iso and iso.th_ab is not none %}
  <p class="gfx-cap">ISO zone boundaries for this machine{% if iso.threshold_note %} ({{ iso.threshold_note }}){% endif %}. <b>No value is marked</b> — the reading did not pass the data-quality gate, so it is not placed on this scale. The measured figure is in the Machine Details table.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% elif iso and iso.th_ab is not none and iso.severity_rms is not none %}
  <p class="gfx-cap">Overall vibration <b>{{ "%.2f"|format(iso.severity_rms) }} mm/s</b>, marked at its measured position on {% if custom_basis %}the machine-specific limits scale{% else %}this machine's ISO zone scale{% endif %}.{% if iso.margin_to_next_boundary is not none and next_zone %} Computed margin to the next boundary: <b>{{ "%.2f"|format(iso.margin_to_next_boundary) }} mm/s</b> below the {{ iso.iso_zone }}&#8201;→&#8201;{{ next_zone }} boundary at {{ "%g"|format(next_boundary) }} mm/s.{% endif %}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if iso and not no_diagnosis %}
  <div class="axes"><span class="muted">Per-axis velocity</span>
    {% for ax in ("x", "y", "z") %}
    {% set v = iso["%s_vel_mms"|format(ax)] %}
    {% if v is not none %}<span>{{ ax | upper }} <b>{{ "%.2f"|format(v) }}</b> mm/s</span>{% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
  {{ iso_gate_crossref }}
</section>

{# ── 3 · Diagnosis ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<section>
{% if insufficient %}
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Diagnosis") }}
  <div class="finding">
    <header><h3>Insufficient data — no diagnosis made.</h3></header>
    <p>The reading did not pass quality checks, so no fault assessment is possible. See <em>Recommended Follow-up Measurements</em> for exactly what to collect next.</p>
  </div>
{% elif analysis_failed %}
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Diagnosis") }}
  <div class="finding">
    <header><h3>Analysis failed — no diagnosis made.</h3></header>
    <p>The fault screen did not complete on this reading, so no fault family was assessed and nothing was ruled out. The measurement itself passed the data-quality checks: this is a failure of the analysis, not of the data. Re-submit the reading. <b>The absence of findings below is not evidence that this machine is healthy.</b></p>
  </div>
{% elif no_findings and unmatched_periodicity %}
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Diagnosis") }}
  <div class="finding">
    <header><h3>Committed diagnosis: none — but this reading is not clear.</h3></header>
    <p>No fault signature matched, and no bearing geometry was supplied — so bearing fault frequencies could not be computed and the bearing screen never ran.</p>
    <p>{{ unmatched_periodicity.sentence | md_inline }}</p>
    <p>That periodicity is at no shaft order this analysis models. Something in the machine is repeating at a rate this reading cannot name, and naming it needs the bearing model number, not another measurement. The following WERE screened and came back clear.</p>
    <ul>{% for item in checked_for %}<li>{{ item | md_inline }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  </div>
{% elif no_findings %}
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Diagnosis") }}
  <div class="finding">
    <header><h3>Committed diagnosis: none — parameters within normal range.</h3></header>
    <p>No fault signature matched the evidence in this reading. This is a positive result, not an absence of analysis: the following were screened and came back clear.</p>
    <ul>{% for item in checked_for %}<li>{{ item | md_inline }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  </div>
{% else %}
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Finding & computed confidence") }}
  {% for d in diagnosis %}{{ v2.finding_card(d) }}{% endfor %}
  {{ v2.unexplained_peak(unmatched_periodicity) }}
{% endif %}
</section>

{# ── 4 · Evidence ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Rows are FILTERED, never fabricated: a finding with neither a computed nor an
   observed frequency produces no row at all. #}
{% if evidence_rows %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<section>
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Evidence") }}
  {{ v2.evidence_table_body(evidence_rows) }}
  {{ evidence_graphics }}
</section>
{% endif %}

{# Session REPORT-3 (item 8) — Evidence per measurement point, in roster order.
   Renders nothing on a single-location report, which is every job until
   INTAKE-2 lands the intake that produces a roster. #}
{% if locations %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ v2.location_evidence(ns.n, locations) }}
{% endif %}

{# ── 5 · Also considered — the differential ───────────────────────────────
   The adjudication travels WHOLE. The ratio arithmetic inside it is the
   argument, so truncating it to "Downgraded on amplitude" is a contract breach,
   not an abbreviation. #}
{% if not no_diagnosis %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<section>
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Also considered — differential") }}
  {% if differential %}
  <p class="muted">Also considered:</p>
  <div class="diff">
    {% for c in differential %}
    <div class="tag">Suppressed</div>
    <div class="body"><b>{{ c.label | md_inline }}</b> <span class="muted">({{ c.confidence }} confidence)</span> — {{ c.adjudication | md_inline }}</div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% else %}
  {{ v2.absent("Differential empty",
               "No competing fault was raised and set aside on this reading. The committed call above had no adjudicated alternative.") }}
  {% endif %}
</section>
{% endif %}

{% if damage_stage and damage_stage.fault %}{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}{% endif %}
{{ v2.damage_stage_section(ns.n, damage_stage, stage_graphic) }}

{% if charts and charts.has_channel_figures %}{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}{% endif %}
{{ v2.spectral_section(ns.n, charts) }}

{# ── 8 · Trend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<section>
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Trend") }}
{% if trend %}
  {% if not_assessable %}
  <p>Status: <strong>{{ trend.status }}</strong>, severity <strong>unrated (ISO severity requires velocity data)</strong> over {{ trend.n_days }} days.</p>
  {% if trend.baseline_avg is not none %}
  <p>Baseline (first 7 days) {{ trend.baseline_avg }} → current (last 7 days) {{ trend.current_avg }} ({{ "%+.1f"|format(trend.pct_change) }}%), in the reading's native units. {% if custom_basis %}Machine-specific alarm limit{% else %}ISO §6.5.2 alarm limit{% endif %} not applicable without velocity data.</p>
  {% endif %}
  <p><em>No forward ISO-boundary projection is offered without a velocity-based severity zone.</em></p>
  {% else %}
  <p>Status: <strong>{{ trend.status }}</strong>, severity <strong>{{ trend.severity }}</strong> over {{ trend.n_days }} days.</p>
  {% if trend.baseline_avg is not none %}
  <p>Baseline (first 7 days) {{ trend.baseline_avg }} mm/s → current (last 7 days) {{ trend.current_avg }} mm/s ({{ "%+.1f"|format(trend.pct_change) }}%). {% if custom_basis %}Machine-specific alarm limit{% else %}ISO §6.5.2 alarm limit{% endif %}: {{ trend.alarm_limit }} mm/s.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {# Three states, not two: a projection, a stated refusal, or NOTHING AT ALL.
     A machine already in Zone D has no next boundary, and the report says
     nothing rather than inventing one. #}
  {% if trend.trend_note %}
  <p><em>{{ trend.trend_note }}</em> — no forward projection is offered.</p>
  {% elif trend.days_to_next_boundary is not none %}
  <p>Projected ~{{ trend.days_to_next_boundary }} days to the next {% if custom_basis %}zone{% else %}ISO{% endif %} boundary at the current rate.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
  {# Session HIST-1 — where the readings came from, when that changes what this
     section may claim about them. Placed after the verdict and before the
     figure: a reader meets the trend, then who supplied it. #}
  {{ v2.history_provenance_note(history_provenance, custom_basis) }}
  {% if charts and charts.trend %}
  <figure><div class="plot"><img src="{{ charts.trend.rel_path }}" alt="{{ charts.trend.alt }}"></div></figure>
  {% endif %}
{% else %}
  {{ v2.absent("No trend assessed",
               "This analysis had no reading history, so no trend could be computed and no ISO-boundary projection is offered. A trend needs repeat readings on the same machine.") }}
{% endif %}
</section>

{# ── Before / after comparison — Session HIST-2 ───────────────────────────
   Additive and absent by default: `comparison` is None on every single-file
   report, so the section renders nothing and consumes no section number. #}
{% if comparison %}{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}{% endif %}
{{ v2.comparison_section(ns.n, comparison) }}

{% if causes %}{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}{% endif %}
{{ v2.causes_section(ns.n, causes, cause_heading, cause_illustration) }}

{# ── 10 · Recommended follow-up measurements ──────────────────────────── #}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<section>
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Recommended follow-up measurements") }}
{% if measurements %}
  {% for m in measurements %}
  <div class="rec">
    <span class="chip {{ m.priority | lower }}">{{ m.priority }}</span>
    <div><b>{{ m.technique | md_inline }}</b> — {{ m.purpose | md_inline }}<span class="trigger">Trigger: {{ m.trigger | md_inline }}</span></div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
{% else %}
  <p>None — the available data resolved the diagnosis without further measurement.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

{# ── 11 · Recommendations ─────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<section>
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Recommendations") }}
{% if recommendations %}
  <ol>{% for rec in recommendations %}<li>{{ rec | md_inline }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol>
{% else %}
  <p>No corrective action recommended at this time.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

{# ── 12 · Limitations ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<section>
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Limitations & confidence notes") }}
  <ul>
  {% if limitations %}{% for note in limitations %}<li>{{ note | md_inline }}</li>{% endfor %}
  {% else %}<li>None.</li>{% endif %}
  </ul>
</section>

{# ── 13 · Coverage — Session REPORT-NA ────────────────────────────────────
   What this analysis did NOT assess, one line per family with its reason
   class. Deterministic on every path; the roster lives in report/generate.py,
   keyed to FAULT_COVERAGE_2026-08-31.md §3. #}
{% if coverage %}{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}{% endif %}
{{ v2.coverage_section(ns.n, coverage) }}

{# ── 14 · Data quality ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Verdict, then EVERY non-PASS check in full, then one line for the rest, then
   the whole roster.

   What may be summarised is ONLY `pass` and `not_applicable`. Every other
   status appears above with its NAME, its STATUS and its REASON IN FULL. That
   is not a convention here — tests/test_report_html.py computes it on every
   fixture and fails if a non-PASS check is ever hidden, summarised, folded into
   a count, or demoted into the roster. #}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<section>
  {{ v2.sec_head(ns.n, "Data quality") }}
  <p class="verdict {{ gate.overall | lower }}"><b>Gate verdict: {{ gate.overall | upper }}.</b></p>
{% if dq_notes %}
  <p>The following checks require attention:</p>
  <div class="attn-list">
  {% for check in gate_attention %}
    <div class="attn {{ check.status | lower }}">
      <span class="st">{{ check.status | upper }}</span>
      <div><b class="mono">{{ check.name }}</b><span>{{ (check.reason or "—") | md_inline }}</span></div>
    </div>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
{% else %}
  <p>All data-quality checks passed.</p>
{% endif %}
  <p class="muted quiet">{{ gate_counts }}</p>
  {# A plain section, deliberately NOT a <details>. The prototype folded the
     roster behind a disclosure and forced it open with a print rule; this
     document is only ever rendered to PDF, where a disclosure cannot be
     disclosed — it would either print open (a section with a pointless summary
     line) or hide rows (a defect). See SESSION_V2WIRE.md. #}
  <div class="roster">
    <div class="roster-head">Full check roster — all {{ gate.checks | length }} checks</div>
    <div class="scroll"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Status</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for check in gate.checks %}
        <tr class="{{ check.status | lower }}">
          <td class="mono">{{ check.name }}</td>
          <td class="mono">{{ check.status | upper }}</td>
          <td>{{ (check.reason or "—") | md_inline }}</td>
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </div>
</section>

{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ v2.parameters_section(ns.n, machine_rows, analysis_parameters) }}

{# Session REPORT-2: beside the parameters, as in the markdown twin. #}
{% if fmax_adequacy %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ v2.fmax_adequacy_section(ns.n, fmax_adequacy) }}
{% endif %}

{{ v2.provenance_panel() }}
{{ v2.signature_block() }}
{{ v2.page_footer(deletion_footer) }}

</main>
</body>
</html>
